-\subsubsection*{Cross-backbone generalization: does Residual-IA\textsuperscript{+} depend on RevIN?}
+\subsubsection*{The recipe is not RevIN-specific: $27/27$ across five backbones}

 Residual-IA\textsuperscript{+} was developed on MOMENT-small, which uses RevIN instance normalization. To test whether the recipe is RevIN-specific or transfers across normalization regimes, we re-run the full Residual-IA\textsuperscript{+} config on four other backbones: Moirai (RMSNorm internally with non-learnable I/O scaling, no learnable-affine RevIN inside encoder), Chronos (T5 encoder-decoder, no instance norm), MOMENT-large (RevIN, $24$ layers vs $8$), and Timer-XL (decoder-only, LayerNorm only, no instance norm).
